								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1012.msg10261#msg10261">Quote from: Kinladar on August 19, 2004, 05:34:39 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><a href="http://forums.gucomics.com/viewtopic.php?t=3683" target="_blank">http://forums.gucomics.com/viewtopic.php?t=3683</a><br /><br />Seems Blizzard is already mismanaging the technical side of the game... Granted this is a single thing, but some other interesting beta bugs.<br /><br />I doubt that WoW will be better quality programming than EQ, or EQ2.<br /><br />Same crap, different name<br /></div><br />But Kin, I think the major difference is that Blizzard is working those things out in *beta*.&nbsp; SOE expects the paying customer to be their beta.&nbsp; It&#039;s hard to fault a company for tweaking/changing/retuning things they think cause imbalance before the game is released.&nbsp; Beta is all about discovering and fixing bugs.
						</td>
					</tr>
